 'intro_kicker'=>'Start with the source','intro_heading'=>'A complete mold inspection for West Vancouver properties','intro_paragraphs'=>['A useful mold inspection looks beyond a visible spot on a wall. Mold grows where materials remain damp, so the inspection should consider the moisture source, the affected materials, the size of the concern and conditions in nearby spaces. This helps property owners make decisions based on evidence instead of guesswork.','West Vancouver homes and buildings face persistent rain, ocean influenced humidity, shaded exterior walls and complex hillside drainage. Roof leaks, plumbing failures, window condensation, foundation moisture and poor ventilation can each create different patterns. Our inspection process considers these local building conditions while focusing on what is actually present at your property.','The goal is to explain the concern in plain language. You receive clear observations, photographs when appropriate and practical next steps. Testing may be recommended when it answers a specific question, but it is not automatically added when visual and moisture findings already provide enough direction.'],
