 'process_heading'=>'What happens during a mold inspection','process_intro'=>'The scope is matched to your concern, the property and the areas that can be safely accessed.','steps'=>[['Discuss the history','We review what you have seen or smelled, when it began, known leaks, previous repairs and any areas that cause particular concern.'],['Inspect accessible areas','Visible materials, plumbing areas, exterior walls, ceilings, windows and other relevant locations are examined for signs of moisture and growth.'],['Measure moisture conditions','Moisture readings and building observations help identify damp materials and possible pathways without opening finished surfaces unnecessarily.'],['Consider targeted testing','Air, surface or material sampling may be useful when identification or comparison will change the decision. Testing is explained before it is recommended.'],['Explain the findings','You receive a clear summary of observed conditions, important limitations, likely moisture sources and sensible priorities for correction.']],
 'secondary_image'=>'image/mold-in-corner-door-vancouver.webp','secondary_alt'=>'Visible mold near an interior corner found during a property inspection','detail_kicker'=>'Information you can use','detail_heading'=>'Inspection before remediation planning','detail_paragraphs'=>['Remediation should be based on the location and extent of affected material. Removing finishes too early can spread particles, erase useful evidence and create unnecessary repair costs. A careful inspection helps define the work area and identifies moisture corrections that should be included in the plan.','Inspection and remediation serve different purposes. The inspection documents current conditions and helps establish scope. Remediation removes affected materials or cleans suitable surfaces under controlled conditions. Post remediation verification may then be used to assess whether the agreed work has been completed.','Our recommendations stay proportional to the evidence. A small surface issue caused by condensation may need a different response from widespread impact after a roof or plumbing failure.'],
 'detail_points'=>['Visual findings documented in context','Moisture conditions reviewed before repair planning','Testing recommended only when it adds useful information','Specialty inspection options for attics, crawl spaces, condos and commercial buildings','Practical priorities explained in plain language'],
 'local_heading'=>'Local mold inspection across West Vancouver','local_paragraphs'=>['We provide mold inspection in West Vancouver neighbourhoods from Ambleside and Dundarave to Caulfeild, Eagle Harbour, Horseshoe Bay and the British Properties. Local terrain, tree cover, building age and exposure can influence where moisture collects and how quickly materials dry.','Properties near the waterfront may experience different humidity and exposure conditions from homes at higher elevations. Older houses can have additions or concealed assemblies from several renovation periods, while newer homes may include complex envelopes and mechanical systems. Each inspection begins with the actual building rather than a standard assumption.','Service is available for detached homes, townhomes, condos, rental properties, strata buildings and commercial spaces. Access and reporting can be coordinated with owners, tenants, property managers and other authorized representatives.'],
