 'faq_heading'=>'Mold inspection questions from West Vancouver property owners','faqs'=>[['How long does a mold inspection take?','The time depends on property size, access and the number of areas involved. A focused inspection may be shorter, while several floors, attics, crawl spaces or commercial areas require more time.'],['Is mold testing included with every inspection?','No. Testing is recommended when results will help answer a specific question or guide a decision. Many visible moisture concerns can be assessed without routine sampling.'],['Can you find mold behind walls?','An inspection can identify moisture patterns and signs that suggest concealed impact. No method can confirm every hidden condition through finished materials. Selective opening may be recommended when the evidence supports it.'],['Should I clean visible mold before the inspection?','Avoid disturbing or painting over the area before it is assessed. Undisturbed conditions and photographs of earlier changes can provide useful information.'],['Do you inspect homes before purchase?','Yes. A mold focused inspection can investigate concerns identified during a general home inspection or areas with staining, odours, past leaks or elevated moisture.'],['What happens after the inspection?','The findings help determine whether moisture correction, cleaning, removal, further testing or specialist review is appropriate. The recommended next step depends on the evidence at the property.']]
